!script {{
  --/| ==========================================================================
  --/| Tutorial 15: Beacon attribute;set
  --/|
  --/| PURPOSE
  --/| attribute;set is an existing ScriptCards function, but Beacon mode gives
  --/| it several additional jobs. This tutorial shows what makes it different
  --/| from !a and !c when beaconsheet is enabled.
  --/|
  --/| HOW TO USE IT
  --/| 1. Select a D&D 2024 Beacon character.
  --/| 2. For the repeating-row example, an NPC with at least one normal Action
  --/|    is best. The rest of the tutorial still works without an Action row.
  --/| 3. Run the ScriptCard.
  --/| 4. Every temporary value created or changed by the tutorial is restored or
  --/|    deleted before the script finishes.
  --/|
  --/| THE BASIC FUNCTION FORM
  --/| attribute;set receives three important pieces of information:
  --/|
  --/| character ID ; attribute name or Beacon path ; value
  --/|
  --/| WHAT !c DOES IN BEACON MODE
  --/| !c is the normal writer for an EXISTING native alias, structured primitive
  --/| leaf, or typed-collection primitive field.
  --/|
  --/| Plain !c requires the final field to already exist.
  --/|
  --/| WHAT !a DOES IN BEACON MODE
  --/| !a is the attribute-style compatibility writer. It handles existing native
  --/| aliases, custom user. values, and familiar repeating attribute-style names.
  --/| A leading ! authorizes !a to create a missing custom value.
  --/|
  --/| Structured paths containing -> do not belong in !a.
  --/|
  --/| WHAT attribute;set ADDS
  --/| In Beacon mode attribute;set can:
  --/|
  --/| set an existing native value;
  --/| create or update a custom user. value;
  --/| set an existing structured primitive field;
  --/| create a missing FINAL primitive field when the rest of the structured
  --/| path is valid;
  --/| set or create a primitive field on an existing Beacon repeating row;
  --/| delete custom, structured, or repeating fields when the supplied value is
  --/| empty.
  --/|
  --/| If deleting the meaningful fields leaves a native repeating row empty,
  --/| ScriptCards can remove that empty canonical row as well.
  --/|
  --/| WHY NOT USE attribute;set FOR EVERYTHING?
  --/| !c and !a make the author's intention clearer and preserve the normal
  --/| ScriptCards command style. Use attribute;set when you specifically need
  --/| its broader creation or deletion behavior, or when adapting code that
  --/| already uses the function.
  --/|
  --/| IMPORTANT
  --/| An empty value can mean DELETE on Beacon surfaces handled by this function.
  --/| Be deliberate when the final parameter is empty.
  --/|
  --/| This tutorial deliberately uses temporary names beginning with scTutorial
  --/| and removes them before it finishes.
  --/| ==========================================================================

  --#beaconsheet|1
  --#sourcetoken|@{selected|token_id}
  --#title|[*S:character_name] - attribute;set Tutorial

  --&CharacterID|[*S:character_id]
  --=OriginalHP|[*S:hp]

  --=TestHP|[$OriginalHP.Raw] - 1
  --?[$OriginalHP.Raw] -le 0|[
    --=TestHP|[$OriginalHP.Raw] + 1
  --]|

  --+|[c][b]1. Existing Native Value[/b][/c]

  --+Starting HP|[$OriginalHP.Raw]

  --/| hp already exists, so attribute;set can route this as a native Beacon write.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];hp;[$TestHP.Raw]

  --+HP After Write|[*S:hp]

  --/| Restore the exact starting value immediately.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];hp;[$OriginalHP.Raw]

  --+Restored HP|[*S:hp]

  --+|[c][b]2. Create and Delete a Custom Value[/b][/c]

  --/| An explicit user. name makes it clear that this is custom script storage.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];user.scTutorialAttributeSet;Created by Tutorial 15

  --+Custom Value|[*S:user.scTutorialAttributeSet]

  --/| With attribute;set, an empty value deletes this custom item.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];user.scTutorialAttributeSet;

  --+After Delete|[*S:user.scTutorialAttributeSet:::Not found]

  --+|[c][b]3. Create a Missing Structured Leaf[/b][/c]

  --/| sheet->settings already exists. The final scTutorialAttributeSet field
  --/| does not need to exist beforehand when attribute;set is used.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];sheet->settings->scTutorialAttributeSet;Temporary structured value

  --+Created Structured Value|[*S:sheet->settings->scTutorialAttributeSet]

  --/| An empty value removes the temporary structured leaf.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];sheet->settings->scTutorialAttributeSet;

  --+After Structured Delete|[*S:sheet->settings->scTutorialAttributeSet:::Not found]

  --+|[c][b]4. Existing Beacon Repeating Row[/b][/c]

  --&ActionCount|[*R:[&CharacterID]:repeating_npcaction:rowcount]

  --?"[&ActionCount]" -eq "0"|NoRepeatingExample

  --Rfirst|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction
  --&RowID|[*R:xxxActionIDxxxx]
  --&ActionName|[*R:name]

  --+Action Used|[&ActionName]
  --+Row ID|[&RowID]

  --/| The row already exists, but scTutorialAttributeSet does not. The function
  --/| can create that final primitive field on the canonical Beacon row.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction_[&RowID]_scTutorialAttributeSet;Temporary row value

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&RowID]

  --+Temporary Row Field|[*R:scTutorialAttributeSet]

  --/| Delete only the temporary field. The real Action row remains.
  --~|attribute;set;[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction_[&RowID]_scTutorialAttributeSet;

  --Rbysectionid|[&CharacterID];repeating_npcaction;[&RowID]

  --+After Row Field Delete|[*R:scTutorialAttributeSet:::Not found]

  --^Summary|

  --:NoRepeatingExample|
  --+Repeating Example|Skipped because this character has no repeating_npcaction rows.

  --:Summary|
  --+|[c][b]When Should I Use Each Writer?[/b][/c]

  --+Beacon !c|Best for existing native aliases, structured paths, and typed fields.
  --+Beacon !a|Best for custom values and familiar attribute-style repeating writes; also supports existing native aliases for compatibility.
  --+attribute;set|Use when you need its broader function behavior, especially missing final primitive creation or verified deletion.

  --+|[c][b]Finished[/b][/c]

  --+Result|Native, custom, structured, and repeating attribute;set behavior was demonstrated and all tutorial changes were cleaned up.
}}
